    "long_instructions": "#The Setup\r\n\r\nMake Anything Wrapped. Pick a topic — sports, grades, a hobby, anything that has numbers behind it. Your program will collect the story, then turn it into a personalized recap.\r\n\r\n1. **Your Variables:** Use `input()` to collect your name, topic, and the raw numbers you'll need.\r\n2. **The Math:** Calculate at least 2 meaningful values. Give each one a comment describing what it is.\r\n3. **The Output:** Test your calucations by printing them to the console\r\n4. **Save to your Backpack:** Once everything is working as expected, save your python file to your backpack. See instructions below.\r\n\r\n::: details [**How do I save to my Backpack?**]\r\n1. Click the 3 dots next to the `main.py` file.\r\n2. Select the \"Save to Backpack\"\r\n   \r\n<img src=\"https://images.code.org/d77df737aa8638aaf5fb1219dd6ee182-Screenshot 2026-09-10 113239.png\" width=\"200px\">\r\n:::",
